Trails — Knowledge to learn and use (@trails: 0, is #chapter, #contains @plan-ergon, #contains @plan-scholazein, #contains @plan-ascholia, #contains @plan-lince, #contains @plan-first-connected-pathways) { r_7A4AY51TXG87NVHR9J1XNZTJQ9
## One body of knowledge, several entrances

Build substantial knowledge from books, articles, methods, explanations, and examples. Support learning, investigation, making, maintenance, and the continuation of knowledge. Philosophy, Sociology, Literature, History, Political-Economy, and Ergon contribute their own questions and connections.

| Umbrella | Branches and file homes |
| --- | --- |
| Ergon — useful labor and productive knowledge | `ergon/`: Hephaestus, Gaia, and connections across productive systems |
| Hephaestus, within Ergon | `ergon/hephaestus/`: mathematics, hard sciences, engineering, computing, astronomy, materials, utilities, production, logistics, maintenance, and shared inquiry |
| Gaia, within Ergon | `ergon/gaia/`: Earth and environment, biology, food and agriculture, medicine and care |
| Scholazein | `scholazein/`: philosophy, history, sociology, political-economy, literature, and art |
| Ascholia | `ascholia/`: bureaucracy and practical administration |
| Lince | `lince/`: ecosystem documentation, habits, simulations, and shared examples |

These are useful homes, not exclusive boundaries or prerequisites. Shared Records remain reusable through ordinary links. Hephaestus names the hard-science branch previously called STEM; Ergon names the broader work of sustaining life and productive knowledge. Astronomy and astrophysics belong with Hephaestus; Earth and environmental studies keep their Gaia home while connecting to physics, chemistry, and engineering.

“Trail” is our name for this plan, the content under `institute/trails/`, and the ordinary Lince data and referenced material it develops. Readers use Records, links, resources, Protein, and normal actions. They do not need to learn a separate Trail feature.

## Connections and selection

Connect a previous Record to its continuations through ordinary assertions using a meaningful predicate. A predicate can be named philosophy, Greek philosophy, farming, or another appropriate name; no reserved suffix or special Record identity is required. Publish its Concept identity with the content so queries preserve its meaning across Organs.

A Protein selects the Records at either end of matching assertions and includes the matching connections. Incoming and outgoing are views of the same stored assertion; do not author a reverse assertion merely to make an incoming link visible. The selected predicates define the boundary. Other references remain available without automatically joining the selected learning or doing sequence.

A Record may participate in several selections and lead to different continuations through different predicates. Shared roots, branches, convergence, revisits, and returns use those same features. Broader selections can combine predicates through normal Protein conditions or an explicitly defined vocabulary family. Names alone do not establish inclusion.

Arrange useful introductions and deeper work with these connections and concise reading guidance. Learning assumptions, exercises, research demands, and completion criteria belong to the particular material when useful. Referencing or combining existing content requires no qualification, additional assignment, formal brief, or special integration process. There is no target count or size.

Protein filters data available through its source. Resolve references and retrieve external definitions through normal source and Sync workflows; discovery imports do not define the selected route or create personal operational data. Viewing or retrieving data does not enact its actions.

For developed learning material, prefer a Record per descriptively named `.lingua` file, with its content and outgoing assertions together. This development register keeps its general guidance and planned Records together in `institute/trails/lince/Trails.lingua`. Group related Records in useful directories and keep source descriptions beside their referenced material. Imports provide discovery; directories and filenames do not establish learning order. Readers follow ordinary links or configure a Protein in their workspace. Published content requires no query files, views directory, manifest, or special Trail feature.

Begin with an accessible primary reading and introduce the understanding it uses. Divide large works into explicit successive reading sections; name what is complete and what is selected. Deepen through connected arguments, language and translation, competing interpretations, sustained investigation, and criticism and revision. Keep those intellectual demands in the relevant material rather than turning them into authoring bureaucracy or software gates. Short paths can remain short when their stated scope is small.

## Sources and explanations

Prefer open, preservable sources. Identify authors, editions, languages, relevant passages, attribution, reuse terms, and actual availability. Keep external references, retained copies, and local alternatives clear. Preserve source identities and valid references when exporting a selection.

Write the explanation the reader needs to connect the material. Introduce notation or assumed knowledge where it is used, and link useful foundations. Reuse Records freely. Add explanations and examples where they help; their presence is an editorial choice.

Easy entrances can lead to demanding work. For Greek philosophy, a survey, close textual reading, working Greek, scholarly disagreement, sustained studies, and independent research describe different depths of study. These demands govern the claim made by that learning material; they do not govern permission to reference it.

Use evidence appropriate to the subject: reasoning in mathematics, methods and observations in empirical work, source criticism in history, arguments and objections in philosophy, and passages and form in literature. When comparing academic material, distinguish actual course bibliographies, programme descriptions, and individual research outputs.

For practical work, describe relevant inputs, skills, equipment, quantities, energy, transport, maintenance, losses, recovery, and cooperation. Link important upstream and supporting knowledge without making the learner reproduce every industry.

Assess potentially hazardous or dual-use material before developing it, including the effect of combining Records, exercises and cited passages. Follow applicable safety boundaries. Where operational detail would enable serious harm, keep a brief account of the topic's importance and scientific context, with a concise, relevant caution. Apply the same judgment to source selections and reused material; links must not serve as a workaround for unsafe instructions.

Use benign examples, simulations, published observations and analysis to develop understanding safely. Keep practical work within appropriate competence, facilities and safeguards. Completion means a connected, accurate understanding of the field within these limits; it never requires dangerous experimentation or the publication of unsafe procedures.

When a stop involving sensitive material is reported, mark the specific unfinished portion as **TODO — sensitive data** in its developed trail and its planning Record here, then continue with the next available task. Keep the reason and remaining safe scope explicit. A deferred portion stays unfinished; revisit it only within the safety guidance.

## Content development and verification

Choose a useful subject, select sources, write or reuse Records, and connect them with meaningful assertions. Check the actual passages and explanations, publish a useful selection through normal Sync/source workflows, then correct and deepen it.

App verification carried forward from the content plan: rerun the frontend check and source/Sync view tests; an earlier check was blocked by unrelated desktop focus, magnification, and compositor compilation errors. Check keyboard link navigation, incoming-link display, source opening and return, and workspace restoration. Playback checks follow any audio or video material being published.

The linked planning Records describe knowledge to develop. ERG labels are editorial references, not Record UIDs, learning order, or a limit. A scope can support several selections, and one selection can use several scopes.

