**Existing entrance:** [Hephaestus](../ergon/hephaestus/Hephaestus.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001).

**Content home:** `institute/trails/ergon/hephaestus/`.

This is the home of the former STEM hard-science plans: mathematics, physics, chemistry, engineering, computing, astronomy, materials, energy, manufacturing, logistics, facilities, and maintenance, with shared inquiry and learning methods. Start from [Hephaestus](../ergon/hephaestus/Hephaestus.lingua). Develop each subject in a descriptive subdirectory beneath its field directory. Pure theory belongs here as fully as its applications; immediate industrial usefulness is not a requirement.

**Development handoff — 30 October 2026:** The objective remains the complete Hephaestus formation, from accessible beginnings through advanced theory, production systems and independent scholarly work. At this checkpoint, 134 planned subjects remain across the sixteen groups below. This inventory is not a limit on coverage. The current unfinished subject is [ERG-181, Clean manufacturing and contamination control](Trails.lingua#r_47NQ213DRJK1AMKQX7DTXR8E6X); its handoff below identifies the exact continuation and remaining work. Continue one subject at a time, preserving shared foundations and the full scope of the other planned subjects.

The [Ergon development ledger](../../anicca/Ergon.md) contains earlier completed subjects, source-inspection limits, verification evidence and detailed checkpoints. Read it alongside the current Records and worktree; historical counts describe their checkpoints, not necessarily the latest files. The latest qualification-and-monitoring checkpoint is verified. Its next specialist-manufacturing extension has not yet been started.

