Mathematical foundations, logic, and proof (@plan-mathematical-foundations-logic-and-proof: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_1K7J2A99Z4798HQEQ7Z0CKWAE7
**Editorial reference:** ERG-012.

Foundations asks what mathematical statements mean and what justifies accepting them. This material covers logic, sets, axioms, proof, infinity, computability, and foundational approaches such as type and category theory, connecting informal reasoning with formal systems and their limits.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_1K7J2A99Z4798HQEQ7Z0CKWAE7

Algebra (@plan-algebra: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_3TKT81FRMZKC1D63FV1RHY8DCJ
**Editorial reference:** ERG-013.

Algebra studies operations, equations, and the structures that organise them. The material progresses from symbolic manipulation to groups, rings, fields, modules, symmetry, and representation, connecting arithmetic and computation with the common structures appearing throughout mathematics and physics.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_3TKT81FRMZKC1D63FV1RHY8DCJ

Linear and multilinear algebra (@plan-linear-and-multilinear-algebra: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_4C8YDS3J7HYQNE68NZX2EEFHGN
**Editorial reference:** ERG-014.

Linear algebra studies vector spaces and transformations; multilinear algebra extends that language to interacting quantities and tensors. This material covers matrices, linear systems, eigenvalues, decompositions, inner products, and tensor representations, connecting geometry, mechanics, computation, and data analysis.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_4C8YDS3J7HYQNE68NZX2EEFHGN

Number theory (@plan-number-theory: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_74PAJV119ZN0GRE3RPCCPGD8Q3
**Editorial reference:** ERG-015.

Number theory studies integers, primes, divisibility, arithmetic patterns, and solutions to equations. This material connects elementary arithmetic with algebraic and analytic methods, finite fields, Diophantine problems, arithmetic geometry, and computational investigations, including connections to coding and cryptography.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_74PAJV119ZN0GRE3RPCCPGD8Q3

Discrete mathematics and combinatorics (@plan-discrete-mathematics-and-combinatorics: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_6NJKZBXXX36NAX3FDKFKEGCXQ4
**Editorial reference:** ERG-016.

Discrete mathematics studies objects that can be counted, arranged, and related by finite rules. This material covers counting, recurrences, generating functions, extremal arguments, discrete structures, and combinatorial designs, connecting proof to questions about arrangements, allocations, algorithms, and finite possibilities.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_6NJKZBXXX36NAX3FDKFKEGCXQ4

Graphs, networks, and discrete relationships (@plan-graphs-networks-and-discrete-relationships: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_71FC22AAFF4VJ4AMPEGYVJWA17
**Editorial reference:** ERG-017.

Graph theory represents objects and their relationships through vertices, edges, and more general network structures. The material studies connectivity, paths, flows, matching, colouring, and graph algorithms, connecting transportation, circuits, ecosystems, communication, and production dependencies through shared mathematical models.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_71FC22AAFF4VJ4AMPEGYVJWA17

Geometry (@plan-geometry: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_76B5P2QMTDB7ED93FDFK3W954T
**Editorial reference:** ERG-018.

Geometry studies shape, position, size, curvature, and the structure of spaces. This material connects Euclidean, analytic, projective, differential, algebraic, convex, and computational viewpoints, showing how geometric reasoning supports surveying, physical theories, imaging, design, and the manufacture of objects.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_76B5P2QMTDB7ED93FDFK3W954T

Topology (@plan-topology: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_246NMRJK7MZRA0HVPG0D58F815
**Editorial reference:** ERG-019.

Topology studies continuity and properties that survive continuous deformation. The material introduces spaces, compactness, connectedness, manifolds, and algebraic ways to distinguish shapes, connecting surfaces, knots, global geometry, physical systems, and data within one broad area of study.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_246NMRJK7MZRA0HVPG0D58F815

Calculus and vector analysis (@plan-calculus-and-vector-analysis: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_3162WTR2P83XKAKSGCKV4486EV
**Editorial reference:** ERG-020.

Calculus studies change, local behaviour, and accumulation. This material covers derivatives, integrals, series, multivariable calculus, gradients, fluxes, and integral theorems, relating their assumptions to motion, fields, growth, conservation, and the balances used throughout science and engineering.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_3162WTR2P83XKAKSGCKV4486EV

Real and complex analysis (@plan-real-and-complex-analysis: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_6MBY9DSF31HHBZ7RV8CGJZAK3X
**Editorial reference:** ERG-021.

Analysis establishes rigorous accounts of limits, continuity, convergence, differentiation, and integration. This material develops real-variable and complex-variable methods, measure theory, analytic functions, and asymptotic reasoning, explaining why familiar calculations work and how analysis extends beyond elementary calculus.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_6MBY9DSF31HHBZ7RV8CGJZAK3X

Functional and harmonic analysis (@plan-functional-and-harmonic-analysis: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_1H74W8BF6ZVMKCG68HEP4ABYBC
**Editorial reference:** ERG-022.

Functional analysis studies spaces of functions and their operators; harmonic analysis studies frequency decompositions and related structures. The material connects norms, spectra, Fourier methods, distributions, and weak formulations with differential equations, signals, quantum theory, approximation, and inverse problems.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_1H74W8BF6ZVMKCG68HEP4ABYBC

Differential equations and dynamical systems (@plan-differential-equations-and-dynamical-systems: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_448403JJMVPXKMBJKADBGVXNWN
**Editorial reference:** ERG-023.

Differential equations describe rates and relationships; dynamical systems study evolution and qualitative behaviour. This material joins ordinary and partial equations, boundary conditions, stability, bifurcations, chaos, and multiscale models, connecting mathematical methods with physical, biological, and engineered processes.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_448403JJMVPXKMBJKADBGVXNWN

Probability and stochastic processes (@plan-probability-and-stochastic-processes: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_7CDRN3668AN4H1PGAM2VYBRDQ4
**Editorial reference:** ERG-024.

Probability provides a language for uncertain events, random quantities, and dependence. This material develops distributions, conditional reasoning, limit theorems, and stochastic processes, connecting mathematical foundations with random walks, queues, diffusion, reliability, populations, and other systems where variability matters.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_7CDRN3668AN4H1PGAM2VYBRDQ4

Statistics and inference (@plan-statistics-and-inference: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_25MTMT0Q4Y4W5NX5X9AJQ8V393
**Editorial reference:** ERG-025.

Statistics studies how limited observations support estimates, comparisons, predictions, and decisions. The material includes sampling, Bayesian and frequentist reasoning, regression, experimental statistics, causal inference, and model checking, emphasising the assumptions and uncertainty accompanying conclusions drawn from data.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_25MTMT0Q4Y4W5NX5X9AJQ8V393

Numerical analysis (@plan-numerical-analysis: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_7V52J6PBQGN2JKG2DF4JRBR5HV
**Editorial reference:** ERG-026.

Numerical analysis studies approximate mathematical answers computed with finite resources. This material covers arithmetic, conditioning, stability, linear solvers, interpolation, integration, differential-equation methods, and convergence, connecting numerical results with error estimates and checks on their reliability.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_7V52J6PBQGN2JKG2DF4JRBR5HV

Optimisation and operations research (@plan-optimisation-and-operations-research: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_7C57C37F6Z004CPC870K3CTNPT
**Editorial reference:** ERG-027.

Optimisation studies the best feasible choices under stated objectives and constraints. The material joins linear, nonlinear, integer, stochastic, and robust methods with scheduling, queues, inventory, allocation, and optimal control, connecting mathematics to production, transport, facilities, and resource use.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_7C57C37F6Z004CPC870K3CTNPT

Applied mathematics and mathematical modelling (@plan-applied-mathematics-and-mathematical-modelling: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_1TNNPVRP2TYCN2GW6FYAJYQAW4
**Editorial reference:** ERG-028.

Applied mathematics builds and investigates models of systems outside mathematics itself. This material connects balances, scaling, approximation, inverse problems, sensitivity, and uncertainty with physics, biology, engineering, and social coordination, focusing on useful representations and the assumptions behind their conclusions.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_1TNNPVRP2TYCN2GW6FYAJYQAW4

Information and coding theory (@plan-information-and-coding-theory: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_62S7KWB7MGVWMJ3HRKTMZJ0611
**Editorial reference:** ERG-029.

Information theory studies uncertainty, communication, compression, and the limits of representing information. This material connects entropy, channels, source coding, error correction, and transmission limits with mathematical constructions, providing foundations for communication, storage, inference, and dependable scientific data exchange.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_62S7KWB7MGVWMJ3HRKTMZJ0611

Mathematical cryptography (@plan-mathematical-cryptography: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_43616S50S5ZA8KQES0Y8PQ4M0A
**Editorial reference:** ERG-030.

Mathematical cryptography studies constructions that protect information or establish properties such as authenticity under explicit assumptions. The material connects algebra, number theory, probability, complexity, and proof with cryptographic primitives and protocols, explaining the scope of their mathematical guarantees.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_43616S50S5ZA8KQES0Y8PQ4M0A

Game theory and decision theory (@plan-game-theory-and-decision-theory: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-mathematics) { r_2Z4K5GNESAAA2QEDAD1HSKMC8M
**Editorial reference:** ERG-031.

Decision theory studies choices under preferences and uncertainty; game theory studies interacting decision-makers. This material covers utility, strategy, equilibria, cooperation, incentives, and mechanism design, connecting mathematical models to shared resources, institutions, and coordination while examining their behavioural assumptions.

**Planning context:** [Mathematics](Trails.lingua#r_6PZSEX3MTC14A74R94SJQ67B3C).
} r_2Z4K5GNESAAA2QEDAD1HSKMC8M

Physics (@plan-physics: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-hephaestus, #contains @plan-classical-mechanics, #contains @plan-continuum-and-solid-mechanics, #contains @plan-statistical-and-nonequilibrium-physics, #contains @plan-waves-and-acoustics, #contains @plan-optics-photonics-and-laser-science, #contains @plan-quantum-mechanics, #contains @plan-atomic-and-molecular-physics, #contains @plan-condensed-matter-physics, #contains @plan-soft-matter-and-complex-materials, #contains @plan-nuclear-physics, #contains @plan-particle-physics-and-quantum-fields, #contains @plan-relativity-and-gravitation, #contains @plan-plasma-physics, #contains @plan-nonlinear-physics-and-complex-systems, #contains @plan-biological-physics, #contains @plan-computational-physics, #contains @plan-experimental-physics-and-instrumentation, #contains @plan-radiation-and-medical-physics, #contains @plan-quantum-information-science, #contains @plan-nanophysics-and-surface-science) { r_5SMEYFVBAX3PK39PSDSDPWQYRQ
**Existing entrance:** [Physics](../ergon/hephaestus/physics/Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W).

**Content home:** `institute/trails/ergon/hephaestus/physics/`, with subject directories for the planned pathways.

Proposed branch Record: `@physics-map`. Organising Record: `@hephaestus`.

**Pathways:** Explain and measure motion, energy, a circuit, or a wave; develop more rigorous accounts of a chosen system. Offer qualitative and quantitative entrances; add algebra, calculus, linear algebra, or statistical methods at the steps that actually use them.

**Available:** [Electromagnetism](../ergon/hephaestus/physics/electromagnetism/Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY), from familiar observations, charge, fields, voltage/current and shared mathematics through static boundaries, matter, circuits, induction, Maxwell conservation, relativity, waves, guides, radiation, scattering, computation and physical evidence. Complete technical books and public undergraduate/graduate programmes, three independently checked original calculations and sixteen advanced investigations deepen into an integrated system and independent research. Eleven shared Records retain their distinct electromagnetic continuations.

**Available:** [Thermodynamics and heat transfer](../ergon/hephaestus/physics/thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/Thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer.lingua#r_6KQBZNJM6WNV9A69R3DZY1NH7E), from ordinary thermal observations, systems and shared mathematics through energy/entropy/exergy balances, potentials and equilibrium, thermal machines, conduction, convection, radiation, phase change, measurements and microscopic transport. Complete books and public advanced courses, four independently checked original calculations and twenty-two advanced investigations lead into a performed physical study, an integrated thermal service and independent research/revision. Twenty shared Records retain distinct thermal continuations.

**Available:** [Fluid dynamics](../ergon/hephaestus/physics/fluid-dynamics/Fluid-dynamics.lingua#r_7PQW1WDHK708BFV23MD8ET61VZ), from observed fluid motion, properties, hydrostatics and shared mathematics through conservation, constitutive laws, viscous/potential flows, pipes, boundary layers, instability/turbulence, compressible and free-surface waves, rotation/stratification, interfaces, multiple phases, rheology, transport, computation and physical evidence. Whole books and public advanced courses, four independently checked original calculations and twenty advanced studies lead into a performed experimental programme, an integrated fluid service and independent research/revision. Nineteen shared Records retain distinct fluid continuations.

