**Planning context:** [Trails — Knowledge to learn and use](Trails.lingua#r_7A4AY51TXG87NVHR9J1XNZTJQ9).
} r_1YY66H962HAJ5XJQHYJWGZQ0Z6

Medical and clinical sciences (@plan-medical-and-clinical-sciences: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-health-and-care) { r_7HJ8WFCVHVKEB5PT4EWBB8D72E
**Editorial reference:** ERG-110.

Medical science investigates disease, injury, prevention, diagnosis, and treatment through biological and clinical evidence. The material connects pathology, immunology, infection, clinical investigation, and the organisation of care, explaining how research and professional practice depend on laboratories, equipment, supplies, and trained teams.

**Reading now:** [Medicine](../ergon/gaia/medicine/Medicine.lingua#r_6DTDCDP6JQ2AV7S78QPGKM2V65) introduces shared medical vocabulary, tissues, body systems, clinical questions, and evidence. Its developed regional sequence continues through musculoskeletal foundations and orthopedics to shoulder anatomy, function, possible problems, and sustained investigation, using English and Portuguese sources.

**Planning context:** [Health and care](Trails.lingua#r_1YY66H962HAJ5XJQHYJWGZQ0Z6).
} r_7HJ8WFCVHVKEB5PT4EWBB8D72E

Public health and epidemiology (@plan-public-health-and-epidemiology: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-health-and-care) { r_3BSVZ18VDVSAAXGVRS9W9JZDZV
**Editorial reference:** ERG-111.

Public health studies and supports health at population scale, while epidemiology investigates the distribution and causes of health-related outcomes. This material connects surveillance, study design, prevention, environmental conditions, interventions, and health systems with the interpretation of population evidence.

**Planning context:** [Health and care](Trails.lingua#r_1YY66H962HAJ5XJQHYJWGZQ0Z6).
} r_3BSVZ18VDVSAAXGVRS9W9JZDZV

Pharmacology and toxicology (@plan-pharmacology-and-toxicology: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-health-and-care) { r_73GP5E4MJW4TSQ4GZXMKEJ6B7G
**Editorial reference:** ERG-112.

Pharmacology studies how substances affect living systems; toxicology investigates harmful effects and their conditions. The material connects mechanisms, exposure, dose–response relationships, metabolism, experimental methods, and evidence evaluation with the development and assessment of substances encountered in medicine, industry, food, and environments.

**Planning context:** [Health and care](Trails.lingua#r_1YY66H962HAJ5XJQHYJWGZQ0Z6).
} r_73GP5E4MJW4TSQ4GZXMKEJ6B7G

