Research ethics and professional practice (@plan-research-ethics-and-professional-practice: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-ethics-and-responsibility) { r_0F68XVBQAG2JFA8ME14H9ATCWZ
**Editorial reference:** ERG-006.

Responsible Ergon work considers the people, organisms, environments, and communities affected by investigation and application. This material introduces research integrity, consent, welfare, attribution, conflicts of interest, professional responsibility, and institutional review, connecting technical decisions to accountable practice.

**Planning context:** [Ethics and responsibility](Trails.lingua#r_13ARZACNYPA4ZZHNVDSYG8C1A8).
} r_0F68XVBQAG2JFA8ME14H9ATCWZ

Political-Economy (@plan-political-economy: 0, is #chapter, #planned, #part-of @plan-scholazein, #contains @plan-political-economy-value-production-and-distribution, #contains @plan-markets-organisations-and-economic-coordination, #contains @plan-money-finance-and-macroeconomic-systems, #contains @plan-states-power-and-political-institutions, #contains @plan-public-finance-collective-provision-and-commons, #contains @plan-development-inequality-and-international-political-economy, #contains @plan-history-and-methods-of-political-economy, #contains @plan-political-economy-of-production-and-infrastructure) { r_2WPG1Y767BM24Z0K4BY6Y6T62W
Proposed branch Record: `@political-economy-map`. Organising Record: `@society-map`.

**Pathways:** Study production, distribution, exchange, power, and political institutions together. Enter through a question about work, resources, money, a collective arrangement, or a historical change, and introduce the relevant concepts, accounts, evidence, and formal methods at the depth used. Compare explanations through Sociology, History, and Philosophy.

## Planned pathways

- [Political-Economy: value, production, and distribution](Trails.lingua#r_40G56P5QGFBE8R837HVXQMWK2R)
- [Markets, organisations, and economic coordination](Trails.lingua#r_36S6PP6AZYT11CGX09K042DRGY)
