First connected pathways (@plan-first-connected-pathways: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @trails, #contains @plan-pathway-find-a-question-and-question-the-map, #contains @plan-pathway-examine-a-philosophical-question, #contains @plan-pathway-read-and-interpret-a-literary-work, #contains @plan-pathway-keep-reliable-stock-and-follow-replenishment, #contains @plan-pathway-construct-and-explain-a-mathematical-proof, #contains @plan-pathway-observe-and-explain-a-local-living-environment, #contains @plan-pathway-understand-build-and-maintain-a-low-voltage-instrument, #contains @plan-pathway-investigate-a-historical-change, #contains @plan-pathway-explain-work-power-and-distribution, #contains @plan-pathway-interpret-a-population-health-comparison) { r_3RYVEGQ60GSD3XY3EVQH0JJRED
Develop these first subjects incrementally through sources, explanations, and ordinary learning connections. Describe the depth of study and the evidence supporting a claimed result where useful.

## Useful crossings to author

| Shared material or question | Connected uses | What the bridge should explain |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Arguments and interpretation | Philosophy, Literature, History, Sociology, and mathematical reasoning | The claim, assumptions, source or reasoning, objections, and the different standards supporting the conclusion |
| Work, institutions, and distribution | Sociology, Political-Economy, History, and Ergon | Material processes, social relationships, rules, power, interests, and the scope of each explanation |
| Sources and historical context | Philosophy, Literature, History, and accounts of science | Edition, authorship, chronology, interpretation, later reception, and limits of the surviving evidence |
| Quantities and balances | Stock, chemical processes, water, energy, and economic accounts | The boundary, unit, incoming and outgoing changes, and any conservation assumptions |
| Measurement and inference | Physical and life sciences, production, social research, and health evidence | Method, comparison, uncertainty, relevant population or conditions, and the limits of inference |
| Change and systems | Physical models, organisms, infrastructure, societies, and economies | Rates, feedback, time, scale, initial conditions, and differences between mechanisms or kinds of explanation |

## Planned pathways

- [Find a question and question the map](Trails.lingua#r_5NFNTGG6YY33QA6CPAZA6B13V8)
- [Examine a philosophical question](Trails.lingua#r_348ZV22NJFVQXHA0TAJ3RMNTS1)
